Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:09:54 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/46] flashnext cuda: at --tp 2 rank 0 forks its whole shared
 expert onto the side stream too

The shared expert runs whole on rank 0 at --tp 2 unless the dense split cuts it (FP4-Local at TP2, FP8 or NVFP4 with
TF_FLASHNEXT_SPLIT_DENSE=0). It is local to rank 0 and writes only the shared slot of y, which rank 0 then sums with
the routed slots as before, so the fork and join keep the bits; it joins before the rank sum. This takes rank 0's
extra kernel time (X2 measured about 11% over rank 1) off the critical path. A split shared expert still runs in line.

The side stream is upstream's (8efa0f976, Armin); the idea is MiaAI-Lab's patch
0016-decode-shared-expert-side-stream-and-lane-batched-deltanet (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-RTX-PRO-6000-TernsorFold 57d815c, MIT).
